          <MultilingualTextItem ID="2" CompositionName="Items">
            <AttributeList>
              <Culture>en-US</Culture>
              <Text>NOT YET WIRED INTO Main[OB1]. Generated 2026-08-08 from the real addresses confirmed live in TIA's Device overview after assigning all 3 ET200SP stations (AFT/MID/FWD) to PLC_1's PROFINET IO system - before that, every module showed no address at all. This is the only block in the whole project that references real physical %I/%Q addresses; everything downstream (FC_IoMapper, Valve_Channels_DB) only ever deals with the abstract 1..368 / 1..208 channel numbers in IO_Buffer_DB. Still needs: (1) FB_ValveLoop simulation guard for real-mapped valves, (2) both this and FC_IoMapper actually called from Main[OB1] - see FC_IoMapper's own header comment. Safe to have present unwired: it only touches IO_Buffer_DB, which nothing else reads yet.</Text>
            </AttributeList>
          </MultilingualTextItem>
        </ObjectList>
      </MultilingualText>
      <SW.Blocks.CompileUnit ID="3" CompositionName="CompileUnits">
        <AttributeList>
          <NetworkSource><StructuredText xmlns="http://www.siemens.com/automation/Openness/SW/NetworkSource/StructuredText/v4">
  <Text UId="1">
    // ONE-VALVE DEMO ONLY. The real block copies 368 inputs and 208 outputs from the ET200SP
    // stations. This demo has no stations, so only CM79 (slot 21) is connected, and it uses the
    // CPU's own I/O. FC_IoMapper and FB_ValveLoop are unchanged and still use channels 81-84, 41-42.
    &quot;IO_Buffer_DB&quot;.DI[81] := %I0.0;   // Open limit switch
    &quot;IO_Buffer_DB&quot;.DI[82] := %I0.1;   // Closed limit switch
    &quot;IO_Buffer_DB&quot;.DI[83] := %I0.2;   // Healthy
    &quot;IO_Buffer_DB&quot;.DI[84] := %I0.3;   // Local mode
    %Q0.0 := &quot;IO_Buffer_DB&quot;.DQ[41];   // OPEN command
    %Q0.1 := &quot;IO_Buffer_DB&quot;.DQ[42];   // CLOSE command


  </Text>
</StructuredText></NetworkSource>
